### Corrected CreateLandscape Steps 6-8

Based on R5 findings, the corrected pseudocode for CreateLandscape steps 6-8 is:

```
6. Prepare Import\(\) parameters:
   FGuid LandscapeGuid = FGuid::NewGuid\(\);  // Landscape's own GUID
   TMap<FGuid, TArray<uint16>> ImportHeightData;
   ImportHeightData.Add\(FGuid\(\), MoveTemp\(HeightData\)\);  // R5-CL-2: EMPTY GUID as map key
   TMap<FGuid, TArray<FLandscapeImportLayerInfo>> ImportMaterialLayerInfos;
   ImportMaterialLayerInfos.Add\(FGuid\(\), TArray<FLandscapeImportLayerInfo>\(\)\);  // R5-CL-1: MUST match entry count
   TArray<FLandscapeLayer> ImportLayers;  // empty, fine

7a. Optional material BEFORE Import \(R5-CL-5: engine sets material before Import\):
   if \(!Cmd.MaterialPath.IsEmpty\(\)\) {
     UMaterialInterface* Material = LoadObject<UMaterialInterface>\(nullptr, *Cmd.MaterialPath\);
     if \(Material\) {
       // R5-IM-2: Can't call EditorSetLandscapeMaterial \(not exported\). Set property directly.
       Landscape->LandscapeMaterial = Material;  // Direct UPROPERTY access
     }
   }

7b. Set lighting LOD \(R5-CL-8\):
   Landscape->StaticLightingLOD = FMath::DivideAndRoundUp\(
     FMath::CeilLogTwo\(\(SizeX * SizeY\) / \(2048 * 2048\) + 1\), \(uint32\)2\);

7c. Call Import\(\):
   Landscape->Import\(
     LandscapeGuid,  // First param = landscape GUID \(NOT map key\)
     0, 0, SizeX - 1, SizeY - 1,
     SectionsPerComponent, QuadsPerSection,
     ImportHeightData,
     TEXT\(""\),  // HeightmapFileName \(empty string safer than nullptr\)
     ImportMaterialLayerInfos,
     ELandscapeImportAlphamapType::Additive,
     ImportLayers
   \);

8. Verify success \(R5-CL-3: Import already called CreateLandscapeInfo + RegisterAllComponents\):
   ULandscapeInfo* LandscapeInfo = Landscape->GetLandscapeInfo\(\);
   if \(!LandscapeInfo || Landscape->LandscapeComponents.Num\(\) == 0\)
   {
     World->DestroyActor\(Landscape\);
     LANDSCAPE_ERROR_RETURN\(TEXT\("Import\(\) failed - no landscape info or components"\)\);
   }
   Landscape->PostEditChange\(\);
```

